[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Press {lb} and {rb} together to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and backs out of it.
{south} uses: doors, ladders, mounted guns, and getting into and out of vehicles, which drive with the left stick and steer and aim with the right. Hold {south} to sprint. {east} jumps, {west} reloads and a long press of {west} changes the fire mode. {north} throws a grenade, and a long press of {north} picks the next grenade type.
Hold {lt} to zoom in with a scope or the iron sights, and let go to zoom out. The game's zoom is a toggle, so {lt} clicks it on the pull and again on letting go; if the game ever drops the zoom itself and they get out of step, tap {lt} once. The right stick turns more finely while it's held. On a scoped rifle {up} and {down} change the zoom. Otherwise {up} and {down} step through your weapons, and {left} and {right} lean.
{l3} crouches and a long press of {l3} goes prone; press it again to stand. {r3} raises the binoculars, which also tag enemies, and {rb} switches the flashlight. Hold {lb} for the weapon ring, aiming with the right stick {rs}.
{select} (Tab) shows the objectives, or the scores in multiplayer. Multiplayer chat needs typing: open the on-screen keyboard with {guide} + {west}.
The game saves at checkpoints only. To get quick save (F5) and quick load (F9), which a double tap and a long press of {start} press, add a playercfg.lua to the game folder holding the two lines PCGamingWiki gives: Input:BindCommandToKey("\\save_game","F5",1); and the same with \\load_game and F9.
These are the game's default keys written from memory and not checked in the game (use, fire mode, prone, grenade type, flashlight and Tab especially); the binoculars on B come from a fan wiki. Crouch and prone are pressed, not held, as the game is remembered to toggle them; if your crouch only lasts while the key is down, set the game's crouch to toggle. Compare them with Options → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The Steam app id is from PCGamingWiki; the executable name is from Discord's game list. The gyro's full turn of 8000 is a guess, not worked out; if a turn of the controller doesn't turn the view as far, change it in the gyro settings.'''

